<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Salinas Grandes Confederation</h1><p class="st-meta">1835 CE – 1879 CE (approx.) · capital Salinas Grandes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful indigenous confederation on the Argentine pampas led by the Mapuche chief Calfucurá, which raided the frontier for decades.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1835 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/araucania">Mapuche</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-calfucura">Juan Calfucurá</a> crossed from Araucanía to the pampas and seized control of the Salinas Grandes, the great salt flats on the edge of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-pampa-province">La Pampa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> provinces. After eliminating rival Boroano chiefs at Masallé, he built a confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranquel">Ranquel</a> and other pampas groups.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-calfucura">Calfucurá</a> controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-trade">salt trade</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> routes to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a>, where stolen livestock was sold. His warriors carried out malones, large raids on frontier towns and ranches. He negotiated treaties and rations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Juan Manuel de Rosas</a> and later with the governments of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argentine-confederation">Argentine Confederation</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-buenos-aires">State of Buenos Aires</a>, playing them against each other.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Argentine army defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-calfucura">Calfucurá</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-san-carlos-1872">San Carlos</a> in 1872, and he died in 1873. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-namuncura">Manuel Namuncurá</a> led the confederation until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julio-argentino-roca">Julio Argentino Roca's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert">Conquest of the Desert</a> from 1878 to 1879 destroyed it. Namuncurá surrendered in 1884.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1835 CE – 1879 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South America</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.22%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1835 CE – 1879 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salinas Grandes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Juan Calfucurá, Manuel Namuncurá</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mapuche religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mapudungun</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Calfucurá confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1857&amp;focus=salinas-grandes-confederation" aria-label="Salinas Grandes Confederation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2991 3273 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Salinas Grandes Confederation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3311 3529L3517 3686"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3517 3686h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3311 3529h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3311 3529h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Salinas Grandes. <a href="/atlas?year=1857&amp;focus=salinas-grandes-confederation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

